WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.337
CMMC 2.

2
00:00:01.337 --> 00:00:06.775
0 uses three levels: Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3.

3
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:14.957
The levels connect information sensitivity and contract risk to increasingly rigorous cybersecurity and verification expectations.

4
00:00:14.957 --> 00:00:16.963
Level 1 is called Foundational.

5
00:00:16.963 --> 00:00:26.611
It focuses on basic safeguarding requirements associated with Federal Contract Information and is based on the requirements in the federal contract safeguarding clause.

6
00:00:26.611 --> 00:00:31.889
Level 1 uses self-assessment and affirmation mechanisms under the CMMC program.

7
00:00:31.889 --> 00:00:39.891
It is not a promise that risk has disappeared; the organization is representing that required practices are implemented within the applicable scope.

8
00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:41.787
Level 2 is called Advanced.

9
00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:53.750
It aligns with the 110 security requirements in NIST SP 800-171 Revision 2 for protecting CUI in nonfederal systems and organizations.

10
00:00:53.750 --> 00:01:03.648
Depending on the acquisition and contract, Level 2 may involve either a self-assessment or an assessment by an authorized CMMC Third-Party Assessment Organization.

11
00:01:03.648 --> 00:01:07.759
The solicitation and contract identify the required status.

12
00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:09.875
Level 3 is called Expert.

13
00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:22.506
It builds on Level 2 and adds selected requirements associated with NIST SP 800-172 for environments supporting higher-priority CUI and facing more advanced risk.

14
00:01:22.506 --> 00:01:28.084
Level 3 assessment involves the government assessment function defined by the CMMC program.

15
00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:35.437
An organization pursuing Level 3 must also satisfy the underlying Level 2 expectations for the applicable scope.

16
00:01:35.437 --> 00:01:40.466
The practical lesson is not to choose a level based on preference or marketing language.

17
00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:50.354
Organizations should use current official requirements and the applicable solicitation or contract to determine the required level, assessment type, and timing.
